---
# OPTIONAL per-developer override for the codebase-kg plugin.
#
# You usually do NOT need this file. The project-level config (codebase / root / counterpart) lives
# in the committed graph's `meta` table — see SCHEMA.md §3/§8 — and the tools (MCP server, hooks,
# pre-push check) read it from there. Create this file (as `.claude/codebase-kg.local.md`) ONLY to
# override that for your own clone. By the `.local` convention it is gitignored / not committed.
#
# Reasons to use it: a peer repo checked out at a non-standard relative path, or a custom
# graph_path.

# Short name for this codebase. Used in `<codebase>-only` parity flags. (Default: from the graph.)
codebase: android

# The code root this graph describes (repo-relative — see SCHEMA.md §3).
root: app/src/main/java/com/example/app

# Where the graph lives in this repo. Default (the convention): knowledge/code_graph.db.
# Set this ONLY to override that default for your clone — there is no repo-root fallback.
# (The older key `kg_path` is still read, so a pre-0.2 file keeps working.)
graph_path: knowledge/code_graph.db

# Optional — the paired repo's graph, for cross-codebase parity. Omit for a single-codebase repo.
counterpart: ../app-ios/knowledge/code_graph.db

# Optional language hint for symbol tooling. Grep always works; this only enables
# opportunistic ctags/LSP. Omit if unsure.
language: kotlin

# Advisory post-edit nudge. Set false to silence it entirely.
post_edit_nudge: true

# Nudge once per this many edits to already-mapped source files. (A file that no node covers is
# reported the first time you touch it, regardless of this.)
nudge_every: 5

# The search gate: a Grep/Glob aimed at mapped code is denied with instructions to query the graph
# first, and it keeps asking rather than standing down after one nudge. `warn` sends the message
# without denying; `off` disables it. SKIP_KG=1 in the environment silences it for one shell.
search_gate: block

# Also treat a shell `grep`/`rg`/`find -name` as a search. Set false to gate only the search tools.
gate_shell_search: true

# How many searches one codebase-kg query clears. The allowance is for what the answer did NOT
# name: the files it named are located searches, which are free and never counted.
#
# Two things never spend it: a search already scoped to a file the graph anchors, and an immediate
# repeat of a search that was just denied — the escape hatch for code the graph has not mapped yet.
# No value here can strand an agent.
gate_credit: 3
---

# codebase-kg — local config

Free-form notes for this repo go here (below the frontmatter). For example: subsystems to skip when
building the graph, naming conventions for node ids, or a pointer to the peer repo's checkout path
so `link` can read both sides.

Nothing in this file is platform-specific *to the plugin* — the plugin stays generic; this file is
where this repo's specifics live.
